Z||000000||Dan010||11-10-2001||09:11 PM||||Today I completed wireing the 2.8's aux. engine bay fan to be seperate from the rad's<BR>fan per "Ogre's suggestions and wireing diagram, thank you Ogre!!!!<BR> Recieved the 180 degree thero and cooler switch today also, will install tomarrow.<BR> How many of the 2.8 owerners have install an additional engine bay fan under the grates????<BR> Also,them gauge only 170deg. top, even though I have a 195 thermo installed, sensor,<BR>gauge, or.............<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||11-11-2001||12:52 PM||||The ECM and gauge have their own temp sensors. hook up an ECM scanner and read that sensor. that or use a pyrometer to measuer the temperature of the thermostat neck.<P>Could be the gauge or it's sender. The needle commonly gets knocked loose because of the messed up wiring. <P>With the aux fan running, you probably don't need the fan under the grate so much.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
